{
  "sn56.40:0.1": "Linked Discourses 56.40 ",
  "sn56.40:0.2": "4. In a Rosewood Forest ",
  "sn56.40:0.3": "Looking For a Debate ",
  "sn56.40:1.1": "“Mendicants, take any mendicant who truly understands: ‘This is suffering’ … ‘This is the origin of suffering’ … ‘This is the cessation of suffering’ … ‘This is the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering’. ",
  "sn56.40:1.2": "An ascetic or brahmin might come from the east, west, north, or south wanting to debate, seeking a debate, thinking: ",
  "sn56.40:1.3": "‘I’ll refute their doctrine!’ It’s simply impossible for them to legitimately make that mendicant shake or rock or tremble. ",
  "sn56.40:1.4": "",
  "sn56.40:1.5": "",
  "sn56.40:1.6": "",
  "sn56.40:1.7": "",
  "sn56.40:2.1": "Suppose there was a stone post, sixteen feet long. ",
  "sn56.40:2.2": "Eight feet were buried underground, and eight above ground. ",
  "sn56.40:2.3": "Even if violent storms were to blow up out of the east, the west, the north, and the south, they couldn’t make it shake or rock or tremble. ",
  "sn56.40:2.4": "Why is that? ",
  "sn56.40:2.5": "It’s because that stone post is firmly embedded, with deep foundations. ",
  "sn56.40:2.6": "In the same way, take any mendicant who truly understands: ‘This is suffering’ … ‘This is the origin of suffering’ … ‘This is the cessation of suffering’ … ‘This is the practice that leads to the cessation of suffering’. ",
  "sn56.40:2.7": "An ascetic or brahmin might come from 